      "key": {
        "uuid": "b9fd4cf7_c811280f",
        "filename": "include/usb_pd_vdo.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 303,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-08T20:45:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t have the PD r3.0 spec immediately at hand. What changed across the SVDM and VDO versions?",
      "revId": "af5b495c6d655c97642569f9befd5c7ecf88dabd",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "22a8033f_8b2d1573",
        "filename": "include/usb_pd_vdo.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 303,
      "author": {
        "id": 3773521
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-15T12:57:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "3.0 -\u003e 3.1\nIDH: In 3.1 Connector type took 2 bits (22,21) before in PD3.0 zeros were expected.\nUFP VDO version: 3.0 only 1.0 (000b), 3.1 replaced with 1.3 (011b). \nVConn and Vbus required: New bits in 3.1 bits B7 and B6.\nUSB Highest Speed: Gen4 added in PD3.1 as 100b\nDFP version: 3.0 had Version 1.0 (000b), replaced in 3.1 with Version 1.2 (010b)\n\n3.1 -\u003e 3.2\nDFP version: 3.1 011b - Version 1.3 replaced 1.2 from PD3.1 - 010b",
      "parentUuid": "b9fd4cf7_c811280f",
      "revId": "af5b495c6d655c97642569f9befd5c7ecf88dabd",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2e5035bd_599560c9",
        "filename": "include/usb_pd_vdo.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 303,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-15T14:17:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e 3.1 -\u003e 3.2\n\u003e DFP version: 3.1 011b - Version 1.3 replaced 1.2 from PD3.1 - 010b\n\nI\u0027m looking at r3.2 v1.2, and it still has DFP VDO version 1.2. 011b would be invalid. What spec version are you looking at?",
      "parentUuid": "22a8033f_8b2d1573",
      "revId": "af5b495c6d655c97642569f9befd5c7ecf88dabd",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b5b85f27_1bd6d77d",
        "filename": "include/usb_pd_vdo.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 303,
      "author": {
        "id": 3773521
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-16T10:06:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My bad, 1.2 is correct for now.",
      "parentUuid": "2e5035bd_599560c9",
      "revId": "af5b495c6d655c97642569f9befd5c7ecf88dabd",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6bcf67b8_692cb8fc",
        "filename": "include/usb_pd_vdo.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 326,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-08T20:45:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From the Realtek driver code, it looks like you\u0027re only able to set one value for this VDO, for a particular SVDM version/VDO version, and you\u0027re using version 1.2. That\u0027s not strictly correct from a PD point of view. We\u0027re supposed to downgrade to the SVDM version of the request. However lots of implementations get this wrong, and if the PDC won\u0027t let you do multiple versions, I wouldn\u0027t worry about it.\n\nBut if you can only use a single version of these VDOs, maybe you don\u0027t need to define structs for any other versions. That could make your life a little easier for now.",
      "revId": "af5b495c6d655c97642569f9befd5c7ecf88dabd",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b67a0c1a_db3a64bf",
        "filename": "include/usb_pd_vdo.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 326,
      "author": {
        "id": 3773521
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-14T09:05:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done",
      "parentUuid": "6bcf67b8_692cb8fc",
      "revId": "af5b495c6d655c97642569f9befd5c7ecf88dabd",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "057705f2_f4643ed5",
        "filename": "include/usb_pd_vdo.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 344,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-08T20:45:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "These fields aren\u0027t actually different in r3.2 v1.2. The formatting of the table just breaks out the bits into their own top-level fields instead of having three 1-bit fields inside of a 3-bit field.\n\nThe format of the version field should also be the same, so you should be able to use the same data structure.\n\nI think that means you shouldn\u0027t need separate versions of the DFP VDO struct.",
      "revId": "af5b495c6d655c97642569f9befd5c7ecf88dabd",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
